#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fx: the deterministic half of the software factory.

The factory skill (an LLM) decides *what to ask agents*; this script owns
everything that must not drift: job state and legal stage moves, model routing
(never below Sonnet), the gate, Jira reads/writes and pull requests.

The factory never lives inside a project. Each project, of one or more
repositories, has its own factory repository (factory.json with repos[],
checks/<repo>.sh, knowledge/, logic/, lessons.md; jobs/ stays local), created by
`fx init --project-name <name> --repo <name>=<git URL> ...`. Code is worked on in
throw-away clones under the work folder next to it: one per repository a job
needs, deleted once its branches are pushed, and short-lived clones for reading. Standard library only, Python 3.9+.
Run it from the factory repository:
    python3 <skill dir>/fx <command> ...

Every command prints a JSON object on stdout (human hints go to stderr) and
exits non-zero on failure, so the orchestrator can follow `next` blindly.
"""

